### Platform Revenue Cross-Check (Manual)

NVIDIA reports revenue by two reportable segments (Compute & Networking; Graphics) and by market platform. The automated XBRL segment extraction collapsed platform labels to generic categories, so the segment chart is suppressed. The following table is manually verified against NVIDIA 10-K filings.

| Platform | FY2023 | FY2024 | FY2025 |
|----------|--------|--------|--------|
| Data Center | $15.0B | $47.5B | $115.2B |
| Gaming | $9.1B | $10.4B | $11.4B |
| Professional Visualization | $1.5B | $1.6B | $1.9B |
| Automotive | $0.9B | $1.1B | $1.5B |
| OEM & Other | $0.5B | $0.3B | $0.5B |
| **Total Revenue** | **$27.0B** | **$60.9B** | **$130.5B** |

*Source: NVIDIA 10-K filings — FY2023 (acc. 0001045810-23-000017), FY2024 (acc. 0001045810-24-000029), FY2025 (acc. 0001045810-25-000023). Platform revenue basis.*

**Key takeaway:** Data Center grew from 56% of total in FY2023 to 88% in FY2025 (analyst interpretation of platform revenue trend). This concentration is both the core thesis and the primary risk.

