### WACC Build-Up and Judgment Bridge

| Component | Value | Rationale |
|-----------|-------|-----------|
| Risk-free rate | 4.3% | 10-year US Treasury yield (analyst assumption) |
| Equity risk premium | 5.5% | Long-run historical ERP (analyst assumption) |
| Beta | 1.65 | 5-year monthly beta vs. S&P 500 (analyst assumption) |
| CAPM cost of equity | 13.4% | 4.3% + 1.65 × 5.5% |
| CAPM-implied WACC | 12.9% | 95% equity × 13.4% + 5% debt × 3.1% |
| Net cash / low-leverage adj. | -1.0% | Near-zero net debt and D/E of 0.05 reduce perceived financial-distress risk |
| FCF quality adj. | -1.0% | FCF margin of 44.8% and strong cash conversion support lower business-risk adjustment |
| Competitive-position adj. | -0.9% | CUDA ecosystem and market position appear to reduce revenue tail risk (analyst assessment) |
| Total quality adjustment | -2.9% | Sum of illustrative analyst-judgment adjustments; not statistically estimated |
| **Selected analyst WACC** | **10.0%** | **Analyst judgment — rounded down from CAPM after quality / balance-sheet adjustment** |

Each sub-component is analyst judgment; the decomposition is illustrative of the reasoning behind the 10.0% selected WACC, not a statistically derived estimate. The adjustment is valuation-friendly, so strict CAPM users should rely more heavily on the 12.9% case.

