{# ---- 6. QUANTAMENTAL METHOD ---- #}
## Quantamental Method

### ML Model Summary

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| **Model** | ElasticNet / Ridge regression |
| **Target** | Next-period revenue growth (YoY) |
| **Training Data** | 10-year XBRL financial metrics (FY2016–FY2025) |
| **Validation** | Walk-forward expanding-window, no lookahead |
| **Observations** | 4 usable target values (annual) |
| **Best baseline RMSE** | 0.65 (mean baseline) |
| **Model R²** | Not computed — pipeline reports RMSE only; 4 usable annual observations make R² unstable and not decision-useful |
| **Model Status** | Diagnostic only — excluded from rating |

The ML model has only 4 usable annual target observations — far too few for reliable out-of-sample prediction. The model underperforms or matches naive baselines. Full details in `outputs/model_audit.md`.

### NLP Signal

NLP extraction coverage: {{ nlp_stats.coverage_pct if nlp_stats is defined and nlp_stats else "N/A" }}% (threshold: 50%). Diagnostic appendix only — excluded from the Hold recommendation.

**Use in recommendation:** Neither ML nor NLP signals support the Hold rating. The recommendation is based entirely on DCF valuation, scenario analysis, and analyst judgment.

